# routine — a one-off act in the middle of a walk does not end the recording
#
# Catching a butterfly is not a routine step, and it is not something a replay has to reproduce: the
# recorder leaves it out and carries on. It used to stop the session there instead
# (TinyCreatureRemovedOutcome declared Breaking), so everything walked after it — in the reported
# run, the street, the shop door and the shop — was never recorded at all.
#
# So: catch first, walk second, and the walk must still be saved. Before the fix this visit recorded
# nothing, because the catch came before any prefix existed.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Yard" --period dawn --observe-only "Butterfly"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
strategy succeed

# The one-off act.
goal catch
advance 12 180
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect-verb catch
expect Caught:

# The walk after it. The footer closes the segment and opens the next phase, pinned to the track.
observe "Test Field"
goal move
click button
wait 60
advance 12 180
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect-verb move
expect Moved to:

observe none
click button
wait 60
advance 12 180
click button
wait mode WorldView 90

# Only the walk: the catch was left out, not recorded.
inspect routines
expect-state routines verbs=[move]
quit
